# GNU Stow ignore list for this package.
#
# This file MUST be named .stow-local-ignore and live in the package root
# (which, for this repo, is the repo root). Stow looks in exactly two places:
# <package>/.stow-local-ignore, then ~/.stow-global-ignore. A file named
# .stow-global-ignore *inside the package* is never read -- that was the bug
# this file replaces.
#
# Because a local ignore list completely REPLACES stow's built-in defaults,
# the useful defaults (VCS metadata, editor droppings, README/LICENSE) are
# repeated below rather than inherited.
#
# Matching rules, from Stow.pm compile_ignore_regexps():
#   * A pattern with no "/" matches the BASENAME, anchored as ^(pat)$.
#   * A pattern containing "/" matches the path relative to the package root
#     with a leading slash, anchored as (^|/)(pat)(/|$).
# The second anchoring is why these patterns carry NO trailing slash:
# "^/\.claude/" fails to match both "/.claude" and "/.claude/settings.json",
# which would silently stow the directory anyway.
#
# Stow always ignores this file itself, so it is not listed here.

# --- Repo scaffolding: belongs in the repo, never in $HOME -----------------
^/Makefile
^/README.*
^/LICENSE.*
^/TODO\.md
^/CLAUDE\.md
^/\.stow-global-ignore
^/tests?
^/scripts
^/\.github

# --- Machine-local state ---------------------------------------------------
# Claude Code's per-project settings. Stowing this lands a symlink inside the
# real ~/.claude and pollutes live tool config.
^/\.claude

# --- Shell history: never stow. A symlink here means every command you type
# --- gets written into a git worktree.
\.bash_history
\.zsh_history

# --- VCS metadata ----------------------------------------------------------
# Listed individually rather than as \.git.* so that a future tracked
# .gitconfig / .gitattributes still gets stowed into $HOME.
\.git
\.gitignore
\.gitmodules
\.jj
\.hg
\.svn
CVS
RCS

# --- OS and editor droppings -----------------------------------------------
\.DS_Store
\._.*
.+~
\#.*\#
\.\#.*
